# Findings the `secrets` CI job is allowed to pass over, one exact fingerprint
# per line: commit, path, rule, line number. Every one of them is a fake literal
# written into a TEST so the test has something of the right shape to assert on -
# repeated-hex cache keys in the Python cache suite, and invented console session
# values in the TypeScript suite. None is a credential to anything.
#
# Fingerprints rather than a path allowlist in `.gitleaks.toml` deliberately: a
# path rule would also wave through a real key pasted into any test file later,
# while a fingerprint pins one line of one blob in one commit. A new fake literal
# in a test therefore fails the job until its fingerprint is reviewed and added
# here, which is the cost this file is paying on purpose.

